m--today nonsense\u001b[39m), no validation in CLI. Existing behavior. Not in scope. \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1BPotential concern about how accountant updates holidays: the file \u001b[38;5;153mdata/holidays.json\u001b[39m \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bis inside package; if installed globally as root-owned, editing may need sudo. Could \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Balternatively allow path via env var. Not asked. The issue says \"keep them in a JSON \r\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[22m \u001b[3G   \u001b[2m\u001b[3mfile that accounting can update without touching the code\" — we've done exactly that.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[22m     \u001b[2m\u001b[3mShipped in package. Wait — maybe a subtle point: \"The accountant runs invoicer from \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bthe package (see the README), so it has to work there.\" That strongly signals \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bpackaging. We verified with actual install. Everything done.…\r\u001b[2B\u001b[23m\u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;174m✢\u001b[39G\u001b[38;5;246mthought for 2s)\u001b[39m\u001b[34;1H\u001b[32;3H"]
